      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Eurostar, a train that's almost as nimble as a goblin navigating a maze of tunnels. You'll be glad to know that the weight and dimension restrictions for checked and hand luggage are as follows: checked luggage has a maximum weight of 23kg and dimensions of 160cm x 45cm x 80cm, while hand luggage has a maximum weight of 8kg and dimensions of 56cm x 45cm x 25cm. \n\nNow, about St Pancras International - it's a bit like navigating a goblin's lair, full of twists and turns. The check-in process typically begins at the designated check-in desks, where you'll need to present your ticket and any required documents. From there, you'll need to proceed to the baggage drop-off area, where you can hand over your checked luggage. The station layout can be a bit overwhelming during peak hours, but don't worry, just follow the signs and you'll be sipping coffee at the station's cafes in no time. \n\nAs you make your way through the station, keep an eye out for the signs indicating the platform numbers for your train. It's a bit like following a goblin trail, but with more people and",
